1	# InkOS — Sprint 6 Design Spec: Artists + Schedules + Team Invites + Roles
2	
3	**From:** Vega (Design Agent)
4	**To:** Koda (Feature Builder)
5	**Date:** 2026-04-15
6	**Stack:** Stack A — Next.js 16.2.3, Tailwind 4, shadcn base-nova, dark-first
7	**Sprint:** 6 — Artists, Schedules, Multi-User Invites, Role-Aware Sidebar (Week 13–15)
8	
9	---
10	
11	## 0. Pre-Build Rules (carry all 50 from Sprints 1–5 forward, plus these)
12	
13	51. Migration `20260416000002_artist_schedules_invites.sql` must be confirmed applied before any Sprint 6 UI is written. Dato confirms. Tables needed: `artist_schedules`, `artist_time_off`, `artist_blocked_dates`, `team_invites`, `role_permissions`, `team_audit_log`. Extended columns on `artists` and `studio_members` must be present.
14	
15	52. `role_permissions` is UI-only enforcement. Fetch once at session start via server component, pass as context (`PermissionsContext`). Use `canDo('permission.key')` helper everywhere. NEVER enforce access at the API layer via this table — RLS handles that. Never mutate this table from the app.
16	
17	53. `studio_members` with `deactivated_at IS NOT NULL` are soft-removed. All team management queries MUST filter `deactivated_at IS NULL` for the active members view. Do NOT touch `user_studio_ids()` — it intentionally includes deactivated members (RLS requirement).
18	
19	54. Schedule editor drag-to-create uses `@dnd-kit/core` + `@dnd-kit/sortable` (already installed). No new drag library. If it isn't installed: `pnpm add @dnd-kit/core @dnd-kit/sortable @dnd-kit/utilities`.
20	
21	55. `calendar_color` on `artist` records is the ONE place where raw hex values are allowed in UI (artist-chosen palette). All other color usage remains token-only. The picker shows InkOS's 10 named swatches (defined in Section 14 below) as a custom swatch grid — not a free color picker.
22	
23	56. The public invite-accept page at `/invite/[token]` uses ZERO InkOS chrome — no `AppSidebar`, no `AppHeader`. It has its own `InviteLayout` with centered card, studio branding injected from `get_invite_by_token`. The `(app)` layout NEVER wraps this route.
24	
25	57. `last_active_at` update: call `updateLastActive(studioId)` in every authenticated Server Action and Route Handler. This is a shared helper (`lib/team/last-active.ts`) that issues `UPDATE studio_members SET last_active_at = now() WHERE user_id = auth.uid() AND studio_id = $1`. Not a trigger. Not in middleware (too noisy). Call it explicitly at the start of each mutating action.
26	
27	58. `accept_team_invite` RPC compares `lower(trim(invite.email))` with `lower(trim(profile.email))`. If `email_mismatch` is returned, show the dedicated error state — never the generic error. Include the instruction: "This invite was sent to a different email address. Ask the studio owner to resend to your registered email."
28	
29	59. Role-description copy for the invite modal is locked in Section 13 (Toast Templates) of this spec. Do not invent new copy.
30	
31	60. `commission_default_pct` on `team_invites` only shows when `role === 'artist'`. The trigger handles `profile_id` linkage on acceptance but does NOT copy commission to `artists.commission_default_pct`. Koda must do this in the post-acceptance route handler.
32	
